+Mermaid fences use the existing isolated diagram runtime and fullscreen viewer. Web dispatches them through the library’s code-block override. Native has no block-renderer hook, so the renderer extracts only Mermaid fences and places the existing WebView host between library-rendered segments. Native chat find is the other exception: while it marks an occurrence, the message draws the occurrence's top-level block as its own segment, so selection cannot cross that block's edges until find moves on. Prose marks use the library's `==` highlight, enabled only on that segment with every other `=` escaped; a code block holding the occurrence draws as `HighlightedCodeBlock`, since native code cannot be marked. A message with link definitions or HTML is not split. See [native selection limitations](native-text-selection.md) for diagram grouping and leading inline images. Streaming keeps the last valid diagram visible while the next revision renders.
 
 Native code blocks use the library's copy control and compiled grammars. Web code blocks use `HighlightedCodeBlock` through the library's `renderers.codeBlock` override. The patch also preserves web list numbering and link titles, marks pending parses with `aria-busy` so Find waits for rendered text, and carries link syntax through native and web tap events. Web inline code inside a link inherits only the link colour; its code font, size and background stay intact. Keep link variants colour-only: native pills replace text runs and prevent paths from wrapping; Android pills also use the surrounding block’s font size. The package patch is tracked by [upstream PR #997](https://github.com/software-mansion/enriched-markdown/pull/997); remove the patch when the pinned release includes it.
 
